's dilemma and need to work out the answer under A-FDT as the essay describes it. The two copies have different observations, so my choice is fixed by one node while the other copy's action stays at its prior, which is the split-copies case.\n\nI'm checking whether the payoffs make defection dominant regardless of the other copy's prior, and they do. I'm also weighing whether the two copies could count as the same function up to renaming, but the essay's emphasis on full observation histories and distinct nodes argues against that. So the A-FDT answer is still to submit.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm looking at this as a fictional prisoner's dilemma and need to work out the answer under A-FDT as the essay describes it. The two copies have different observations, so my choice is fixed by one node while the other copy's action stays at its prior, which is the split-copies case.\n\nI'm checking whether the payoffs make defection dominant regardless of the other copy's prior, and they do. I'm also weighing whether the two copies could count as the same function up to renaming, but the essay's emphasis on full observation histories and distinct nodes argues against that. So the A-FDT answer is still to submit.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9380,"completion_tokens":1041,"total_tokens":10421,"cost":0.05834,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.05834,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.03752,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.02082},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":477,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}